A||N||13||bHooper||Difficulty rebuilding a headlight motor..||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||10-19-2000||07:29 AM||||I have been trying to rebuild a headlight motor (w/new gear from 007DOUG).  After replacing the gear (using dialectic grease on all motor parts), i cleaned all conectors/relays/switchs and the motor, with electric motor cleaner.<P>Upon reinstalling the headlight assembly, i had the following problems:<BR>1)with hood up, motor went up fine.  but took 4-5 minutes to go down!<BR>2)with hood down, light took 4-5 minutes to rise, but went down fine.<BR>3)a "dull bell" sound was heard.  im assuming that this was the relay turning on and off.  this continued after the headlight switch/car was turned off.<BR>4)motor was warm to the touch (other motor was not).<BR>5) there is some resistance in the motor... but i am certain everything is assembled right this time.  i ma using tie wraps to hold the shell together (until im certain).<P>Sorry about the length... any thoughts on the problem, are welcome!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-19-2000||09:19 AM||||Sounds like you have some binding in the either the worm gear, or incorrect spacer placement in the drive gear (the large one in the round cage).<BR>Armature binding could be suspect as well.<BR>What did the motor do prior to overhaul?<P>This is assuming the motor is good!<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 10-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||10-19-2000||09:51 AM||||prior to rebuild, the motor wouldnt do much or anything.  i know that it is/was getting power.  sometimes it would wind a bit on its own, while i was manually winding it... up or down.<P>after reassembly, i used 4 or 5 tie wraps to hold the shell together (until i was certain it was right).  i guess that this could be causing some of the problem, but not all.<P>i was kinda thinking it was a bad relay, because it kept switching own and off, and maybe not allowing enough electricity to pass through.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||10-19-2000||01:22 PM||||Suggestion:  Unplug both motors.  Hand crank the "good" motor all the way up, and notice how it feels throughout its travel.  Now go over and hand crank the "bad" motor - if it takes significantly more effort, it's a good bet something is mechanically out of whack (duh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">), and you need to take the motor apart again (yay  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ).<P>If the motors feel about the same throughout their travel, it's probably an electrical problem.    ||||reg||3
Z||000004||theogre||10-19-2000||05:26 PM||||You didn't get any grease/oil on the brushes or armature contacts while reassembling it did you? You don't put anything on there. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||007DOUG||10-19-2000||06:23 PM||||Once you've tried all of the above...<BR>If your motor still won't work, Send it to me, and I'll rebuild it.<P>Sounds like some misalgined gears. The motor should never take 4 minutes to go down, nor should it feel warm.||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||10-19-2000||07:46 PM||||well its not taking quite that long... but i would say it is much slower than the other one... anoyingly so.<P>Doug, I gotta go out of town tommorow, but will try to look at again either sunday night or tuesday (gotta watch the phins on MNF).<P>Thanks,<BR>hoop<P>ps<BR>ogre, i may have done that! wow, i will have to check that!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||zeusrekning||10-19-2000||10:00 PM||||i am having motor problems also. the gear looked ok but the bushing were bad and the thing in side the gear is worn so i made some over sized bushings.reinstalled and it works a day or two then starts the hopping up and down. i was wondering if mabey i was connecting the arm on the motor two the light<BR>incorrectly. Like mabey the motor is in the up position but the light was down.87 coupe pass side. Oh i made the bushings out of uhmw or teflon . it seems like it was teflon. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||10-23-2000||08:45 PM||||Ok, here's the latest.<P>Dismantled and reassembled the whole thing, includeing the switch off of the motor.  I had to solder one contact from the cap that attach's to the brush.<P>Upon reasembly, I installed everything back into the bucket and car.<P>However,when I pluged it all up... it raised up on it's own!  It doesn't even go down, electically.  I still have the "sound" from the switch.<P>I think the whole problem can be wound in the switch!  What do you guy's think?  Can I replace the switch?<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
