Z||000010||bHooper||10-23-2000||11:01 PM||||Rodney, <BR>The gears are fine, now.  I replaced the plastic one with a metal one, it does operate nice and smooth.<P>However the switch keeps turning off and on.  Since I have tried it with both relays, I can eliminate that.  The left motor works fine, so I can eliminate the primary relay.  And the brushes seem to be getting good contact.  I think the cap in the switch is the problem, so I will need a new switch.<P>If I can find one.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
